{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/reviews/id131495225"}, "name":{"label":"Quickquiggers"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2022-06-17T10:57:36-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"5"}, "im:version":{"label":"4.8.3"}, "id":{"label":"8783619012"}, "title":{"label":"An App that cheers me on!"}, "content":{"label":"I love the Pedometer App. \nLet me explain why!  I enjoy walking. As a 76 year old male I aim to walk 4 miles each day - usually early morning before breakfast.  \nMy daily target is at least  10,000 steps. \nA couple of years ago I was diagnosed with cardiac issues including the need for a new aortic valve and a double heart bypass. \nDuring the “waiting for cardiac surgery” I felt it was essential to keep fit and keep walking. I knew this would aid my recovery.  The daily monitoring of my walking with the Pedometer App was automatic.  I was able to easily adjust my target as my health deteriorated - I managed to keep on walking. \nIn March 2022 I had open heart surgery and have had a good recovery.  I’m back to walking four miles each morning and managing around 13 000 steps a day.  \nThe Pedometer App has a brilliant display, it’s easy to read and there are lots of variations on the settings. I love the confetti shower that I get when I’ve achieved my target.  \nI highly recommend this user friendly app.  👏\nPeter S Quigley", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/review?id=712286167&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
